1
00:01:32,979 --> 00:01:35,009
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:37,670
[Episode 2]

3
00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:40,729
On July 1, 1979,

4
00:01:40,759 --> 00:01:41,820
the Second Session

5
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,259
of the Fifth National People's Congress

6
00:01:44,430 --> 00:01:45,430
adopted a resolution
to pass seven laws in one day,

7
00:01:45,430 --> 00:01:47,150
an event known as "Seven Laws in One Day."

8
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:48,590
These 7 important laws

9
00:01:48,759 --> 00:01:50,640
set a record for the most laws passed

10
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:51,640
in one NPC session

11
00:01:51,710 --> 00:01:54,710
since the founding
of the People's Republic of China.

12
00:01:54,979 --> 00:01:56,700
This milestone ended China's

13
00:01:56,729 --> 00:01:59,090
long history of having no criminal law.

14
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:00,390
From this point forward,

15
00:02:00,390 --> 00:02:02,500
our country's legislative work
fully resumed,

16
00:02:00,580 --> 00:02:02,300
[Seven Laws in One Day]

17
00:02:02,860 --> 00:02:05,510
ensuring the smooth progress
of reform and opening up.

18
00:02:05,510 --> 00:02:06,840
It also brought an end to

19
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:08,630
the prolonged absence of laws
in many fields

20
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:10,000
and ushered in a new era

21
00:02:10,030 --> 00:02:13,160
in the development
of socialist democratic rule of law.

22
00:02:23,910 --> 00:02:25,120
Nice! Nice!

23
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:33,800
I've found that milking sympathy

24
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:34,680
is an art.

25
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:37,220
Look at him.

26
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,329
Just look at him.

27
00:02:39,870 --> 00:02:41,120
That torn vest of his.

28
00:02:42,079 --> 00:02:43,400
He doesn't even mend it.
Must be on purpose.

29
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:44,800
He's just waiting for some girl

30
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:46,230
to notice and offer to mend it for him.

31
00:02:46,230 --> 00:02:47,690
Look how worked up you are.

32
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:49,480
Why would I be worked up?

33
00:02:56,750 --> 00:02:57,590
Come on,

34
00:02:57,590 --> 00:02:58,720
Yu Gaoyuan! Come on!

35
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:00,310
Aren't you and Xia Yingjie

36
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:01,710
high school classmates?

37
00:03:01,710 --> 00:03:02,150
Yeah.

38
00:03:02,630 --> 00:03:03,560
Then how come it seems to me that she

39
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,490
doesn't really want to talk to you?

40
00:03:07,250 --> 00:03:07,980
You can tell?

41
00:03:08,470 --> 00:03:09,400
How could I not?

42
00:03:09,750 --> 00:03:10,680
I don't think so.

43
00:03:11,030 --> 00:03:11,910
I can tell.

44
00:03:12,750 --> 00:03:14,150
There's a story there, isn't there?

45
00:03:14,150 --> 00:03:15,030
We're fine.

46
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,030
Yeah, fine.

47
00:03:18,630 --> 00:03:19,560
Awesome!

48
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:20,710
Yu Gaoyuan!

49
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:22,560
Nice!

50
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:27,150
Won't be so fine from here on, I think.

51
00:03:27,150 --> 00:03:28,550
The story's about to end.

52
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:29,680
Come on!

53
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:36,960
Yu Gaoyuan!

54
00:03:37,910 --> 00:03:38,630
Come on!

55
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:41,350
Which student can tell us

56
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,960
the purpose of criminal law?

57
00:03:46,690 --> 00:03:47,280
Sir.

58
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:48,890
Go ahead.

59
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:50,970
First, it's to safeguard

60
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,810
the people's democratic dictatorship
in our country.

61
00:03:52,810 --> 00:03:54,560
Second, to protect
the rights and interests

62
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:55,840
of society and the people

63
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,440
and to punish criminal acts.

64
00:03:57,470 --> 00:03:59,530
Also... to eliminate crime, I think?

65
00:04:02,310 --> 00:04:02,910
Very good.

66
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,340
Any other students

67
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,780
have something to add?

68
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:08,240
Sir.

69
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:11,080
I think the purpose of criminal law

70
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,400
should not only be

71
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:15,340
to protect
society and the people's interests.

72
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,860
Shouldn't it also include

73
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,800
safeguarding the rights
of all parties involved,

74
00:04:20,070 --> 00:04:22,200
especially the rights of the accused?

75
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:28,480
Good.

76
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:31,000
Then, Zeming.

77
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:33,310
If we go by your logic

78
00:04:33,830 --> 00:04:35,270
that the purpose of criminal law

79
00:04:35,270 --> 00:04:36,530
is to eliminate crime,

80
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:39,070
then we wouldn't need to keep enacting

81
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:41,720
criminal law and criminal procedure law.

82
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:43,409
For example,

83
00:04:43,630 --> 00:04:44,390
let's say you're a criminal,

84
00:04:44,390 --> 00:04:45,950
and I'm the presiding judge.

85
00:04:45,950 --> 00:04:47,240
I want to eliminate you—

86
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:48,100
that's simple.

87
00:04:48,310 --> 00:04:49,970
I'll just pin some crime on him

88
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,920
and give him the harshest sentence,
just like that.

89
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:52,630
After all, what you want

90
00:04:52,630 --> 00:04:54,190
is to eliminate crime, right?

91
00:04:54,190 --> 00:04:55,480
So I'll do whatever

92
00:04:55,510 --> 00:04:56,800
is most efficient

93
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:58,180
and intimidating.

94
00:04:58,630 --> 00:04:59,430
Then tell me,

95
00:04:59,430 --> 00:05:01,360
why do we still need criminal law

96
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:03,350
and criminal procedure law?

97
00:05:03,510 --> 00:05:03,920
Right?

98
00:05:04,650 --> 00:05:06,070
They'd only get in the way, right?

99
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:07,400
Chen Yizhong's idea...

100
00:05:08,870 --> 00:05:09,870
is very valuable.

101
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:14,070
But how to balance the two

102
00:05:14,270 --> 00:05:15,600
is a major challenge.

103
00:05:16,070 --> 00:05:17,950
The implementation of these 2 laws

104
00:05:17,950 --> 00:05:19,520
is only the first step.

105
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:23,370
The heavy responsibility of building

106
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:24,880
China's legal system

107
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:26,580
has fallen upon

108
00:05:27,510 --> 00:05:28,120
all of you.

109
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:34,290
Come in, come in.

110
00:05:35,430 --> 00:05:35,950
Zhou!

111
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,520
You owe me a carton of Daqianmen.

112
00:05:41,750 --> 00:05:42,550
Cheng Jianji,

113
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:43,680
what you're doing is a textbook case of

114
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:46,080
extortion and blackmail, I'm telling you.

115
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:47,680
Guess who he is.

116
00:05:50,510 --> 00:05:52,000
My student. Who else could he be?

117
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,110
Your student?

118
00:05:54,230 --> 00:05:55,380
He's Chen Fan's son.

119
00:06:03,830 --> 00:06:05,430
You mean the Chen Fan we know?

120
00:06:05,870 --> 00:06:07,730
D-Do you know some other Chen Fan?

121
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:09,800
He looks like him.

122
00:06:10,390 --> 00:06:11,870
You know what? He really does.

123
00:06:11,870 --> 00:06:13,800
Bigger-built than Chen Fan, though.

124
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:14,660
I didn't expect

125
00:06:15,070 --> 00:06:15,830
Chen Fan's son

126
00:06:15,830 --> 00:06:17,360
to be this grown-up already.

127
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,310
Tell me, is this kid

128
00:06:18,310 --> 00:06:19,630
worth a carton of Daqianmen?

129
00:06:19,630 --> 00:06:20,960
I'll give you 2 cartons!

130
00:06:22,770 --> 00:06:23,430
Yu Gaoyuan,

131
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:24,200
what is it?

132
00:06:24,630 --> 00:06:26,070
Mr. Zhou, I've borrowed

133
00:06:26,070 --> 00:06:26,830
the books you wanted

134
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:27,830
from the library.

135
00:06:28,230 --> 00:06:29,560
Just put them on my desk.

136
00:06:32,430 --> 00:06:32,960
Yizhong.

137
00:06:33,510 --> 00:06:35,070
How is your dad?

138
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:39,730
He's doing well.

139
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:41,310
You both know my dad?

140
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:44,460
Chen Fan is still the same.

141
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:45,930
He just thinks too much.

142
00:06:46,159 --> 00:06:46,950
You'd think that
since his son is studying here,

143
00:06:46,950 --> 00:06:48,390
he could at least say something.

144
00:06:48,390 --> 00:06:49,560
Your dad actually

145
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:51,159
graduated from our school.

146
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:52,450
Back then...

147
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,240
All right, enough about "back then."

148
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:53,640
You...

149
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:55,490
Come by

150
00:06:55,830 --> 00:06:56,600
our place sometime,

151
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:57,830
and I'll have my wife
make dumplings for you.

152
00:06:57,830 --> 00:06:59,490
Her dumplings are delicious.

153
00:07:00,030 --> 00:07:00,440
Okay.

154
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:05,830
What you said in class

155
00:07:05,830 --> 00:07:07,160
really got me thinking.

156
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:10,010
I was just speaking from the heart.

157
00:07:10,010 --> 00:07:11,810
Everyone was exchanging ideas.

158
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:16,180
I heard from Yingjie
that you can play the trumpet.

159
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:17,870
Yeah, I used to play it a lot,

160
00:07:18,430 --> 00:07:19,560
but I don't anymore.

161
00:07:22,070 --> 00:07:22,600
Gaoyuan,

162
00:07:22,870 --> 00:07:23,480
actually,

163
00:07:24,070 --> 00:07:25,870
you're excellent in a lot of areas too.

164
00:07:25,870 --> 00:07:26,870
I really envy you.

165
00:07:27,070 --> 00:07:28,600
Well, I don't have a choice.

166
00:07:28,830 --> 00:07:30,120
If I want to change my fate,

167
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:31,520
I can only rely on myself.

168
00:07:31,630 --> 00:07:32,760
If I don't work hard,

169
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:35,980
who will invite me over
for dumplings in the future?

170
00:07:41,430 --> 00:07:42,760
Here you go, here you go!

171
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:45,020
Cabbage and pork filling!

172
00:07:45,170 --> 00:07:45,870
Come on, eat up.

173
00:07:45,870 --> 00:07:47,120
Eat them while they're hot.

174
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:48,040
Come on.

175
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:48,680
Have some dumplings.

176
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:49,340
Okay, okay.

177
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:50,330
Eat more.

178
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,710
Don't stand on ceremony at our place.

179
00:07:51,710 --> 00:07:52,680
S-Slow down.

180
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:55,180
Are these dumplings good?

181
00:07:55,190 --> 00:07:56,560
I'll wait and eat with you.

182
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:58,040
They're delicious! Delicious!

183
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,360
If they're good, say so already.

184
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:00,190
Delicious!

185
00:08:00,210 --> 00:08:02,070
They're so good! Thank you, Mrs. Zhou!

186
00:08:02,070 --> 00:08:04,210
As long as you enjoy them, I'm happy.

187
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:05,530
Your teacher loves having people over.

188
00:08:05,530 --> 00:08:06,390
Come by often from now on.

189
00:08:06,390 --> 00:08:07,430
There's always plenty.

190
00:08:07,430 --> 00:08:08,360
Okay, Mrs. Zhou.

191
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:10,240
But this time, we still have to
thank Yizhong

192
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:11,800
for bringing us together.

193
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:13,070
Otherwise, I wouldn't have dared...

194
00:08:13,070 --> 00:08:13,560
well,

195
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,510
I wouldn't have gotten to
taste your dumplings.

196
00:08:15,510 --> 00:08:16,710
Come on, eat more.

197
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:19,040
Yu Gaoyuan,

198
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:21,000
you don't need any dipping sauce
with your dumplings, eh?

199
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,090
You're already salty enough.

200
00:08:22,090 --> 00:08:22,600
You...

201
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:24,310
Even dumplings
can't stop you from talking.

202
00:08:24,310 --> 00:08:25,330
You just t-talk too much.

203
00:08:25,330 --> 00:08:26,390
Hurry up and eat
before they all clump together.

204
00:08:26,390 --> 00:08:27,190
Eat, eat, eat.

205
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,010
Gaoyuan.

206
00:08:32,909 --> 00:08:33,960
I heard

207
00:08:34,870 --> 00:08:37,530
you got elected as
the student union president.

208
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:39,820
Yes, thanks to everyone's support.

209
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:41,120
I'm thinking that afterward,

210
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:43,240
we should organize
more social practice activities,

211
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,120
such as bringing legal knowledge
to rural areas.

212
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,000
If we can get in touch

213
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:46,960
with the Supreme People's Court
and the Supreme People's Procuratorate,

214
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:48,910
our student union members

215
00:08:48,910 --> 00:08:50,790
can hold more symposiums.

216
00:08:50,810 --> 00:08:52,150
That way, we can learn more
from our seniors.

217
00:08:52,150 --> 00:08:53,390
Alright, alright. Hurry up and eat.

218
00:08:53,390 --> 00:08:54,120
We can talk about this back at school.

219
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:54,570
No, no, no.

220
00:08:54,570 --> 00:08:55,320
The food will get cold.

221
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:56,980
You all should learn from him.

222
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:58,140
He has great ideas.

223
00:08:58,630 --> 00:08:59,080
Good.

224
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,200
The law must be combined with practice.

225
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:04,040
Thank you, Mr. Cheng.

226
00:09:04,870 --> 00:09:05,320
Okay.

227
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,740
Try some of the dishes.

228
00:09:11,870 --> 00:09:12,440
Mr. Zhou.

229
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:14,770
What exactly happened

230
00:09:14,770 --> 00:09:16,280
between you and my dad?

231
00:09:20,910 --> 00:09:22,200
If you only hear my side,

232
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,400
that'd just be one-sided, wouldn't it?

233
00:09:25,030 --> 00:09:25,750
Sit, sit.

234
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,210
It's all in the past.

235
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:31,810
Right now,

236
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:33,840
there's a shortage of legal talent.

237
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:34,890
Your dad won't be

238
00:09:35,030 --> 00:09:36,560
at the factory much longer.

239
00:09:37,390 --> 00:09:38,450
When he comes back,

240
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:39,390
he and I

241
00:09:40,270 --> 00:09:41,530
will share a pot of wine

242
00:09:41,550 --> 00:09:43,080
and let bygones be bygones.

243
00:09:44,790 --> 00:09:46,590
I still prefer talking with you.

244
00:09:47,030 --> 00:09:48,690
Whenever I chat with my dad...

245
00:09:51,030 --> 00:09:51,550
he never gives me

246
00:09:51,550 --> 00:09:52,610
a straight answer.

247
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:57,680
That's just Chen Fan for you.

248
00:09:58,090 --> 00:09:59,020
Enough about us.

249
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:01,120
I've looked at your transcript.

250
00:10:01,550 --> 00:10:02,150
Very good.

251
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:03,670
In your final undergraduate year,

252
00:10:03,670 --> 00:10:04,960
you'll go do internships

253
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:06,490
and then choose your field.

254
00:10:06,550 --> 00:10:07,480
Are you planning

255
00:10:07,630 --> 00:10:09,030
to start working immediately

256
00:10:09,030 --> 00:10:10,890
or go abroad for further studies?

257
00:10:11,030 --> 00:10:12,000
I could even go abroad?

258
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:12,440
Yeah.

259
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:15,370
West Germany or the United States.

260
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:18,320
Our department gets 3 spots each year—

261
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:20,550
2 for graduate students
and 1 for undergrads.

262
00:10:20,550 --> 00:10:22,440
Then going abroad sounds like
the better choice.

263
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:23,390
I've always felt

264
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:24,570
that our criminal law theory

265
00:10:24,570 --> 00:10:25,550
should indeed draw on

266
00:10:25,550 --> 00:10:26,790
the best of Western thinking,

267
00:10:26,790 --> 00:10:28,630
but even more importantly, it needs to
fit our country's actual conditions

268
00:10:28,630 --> 00:10:30,720
and make the most of our own strengths.

269
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:31,580
That way, we...

270
00:10:35,030 --> 00:10:36,230
Am I talking too much?

271
00:10:36,350 --> 00:10:38,030
You have to be a little arrogant.

272
00:10:38,030 --> 00:10:39,600
If you don't have this bit of
a "who else but me" spirit,

273
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:40,320
you don't deserve to be

274
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:41,320
a student of mine.

275
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,340
However, Yizhong,

276
00:10:44,390 --> 00:10:46,390
the spots for government-sponsored
study abroad are limited.

277
00:10:46,390 --> 00:10:48,270
Grades will decide everything in the end.

278
00:10:48,270 --> 00:10:48,800
I won't be

279
00:10:48,870 --> 00:10:50,390
pulling any strings for you.

280
00:10:50,390 --> 00:10:51,790
Don't worry about that, Mr. Zhou.

281
00:10:51,790 --> 00:10:52,590
I understand.

282
00:10:53,750 --> 00:10:54,210
Good.

283
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,440
I just found this book.

284
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:57,080
Take it back and study it carefully.

285
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:57,440
Okay.

286
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,370
Thank you, Mr. Zhou.

287
00:11:12,780 --> 00:11:15,660
[1983, Beijing City]

288
00:11:16,630 --> 00:11:18,240
The place where we are going
for our internship,

289
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,360
Nanyu—

290
00:11:19,670 --> 00:11:20,960
is it quite close

291
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:21,960
to your hometown?

292
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:23,600
No, it's still quite far.

293
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:24,240
Really?

294
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:27,030
It's been 3 years,
and I still haven't figured out

295
00:11:27,030 --> 00:11:28,830
exactly where your hometown is.

296
00:11:28,930 --> 00:11:31,080
If growing up in that orphanage counts,

297
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:32,240
then my hometown is Guiyang.

298
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:32,790
Guiyang?

299
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:36,410
Is that one okay?

300
00:11:37,630 --> 00:11:39,890
That's an old woman, for goodness' sake.

301
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:44,010
That one.

302
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:48,130
She's already given birth!

303
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:57,480
Let me take it.

304
00:11:57,510 --> 00:11:57,870
No.

305
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:01,110
Those two.

306
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:06,980
The one with long hair is good.

307
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:10,490
You only dare to pick on the timid ones.

308
00:12:12,870 --> 00:12:14,070
You wait right there.

309
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:21,920
Hooligan!

310
00:12:22,150 --> 00:12:22,720
See?

311
00:12:22,910 --> 00:12:23,510
Hooligan!

312
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:24,720
Catch the hooligan!

313
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:26,530
Kiss her on the lips! The cheek won't do!

314
00:12:26,530 --> 00:12:27,460
Hooligan!

315
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,030
-Don't move!
-Help!

316
00:12:29,030 --> 00:12:29,790
Stop yelling!

317
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:30,590
Stop yelling!

318
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:31,730
Catch the hooligan!

319
00:12:31,870 --> 00:12:33,130
-Help!
-Stop yelling!

320
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:33,630
Hooligan!

321
00:12:33,630 --> 00:12:34,080
Let go!

322
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:34,910
Hooligan!

323
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:36,040
Stop yelling!

324
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:37,600
If you keep yelling...

325
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:38,400
Stop yelling!

326
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:39,790
-Catch the hooligan!
-Stop yelling!

327
00:12:39,790 --> 00:12:40,720
Help! Hoo...

328
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:42,320
Help!

329
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:44,790
Leave.

330
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:52,850
Are you okay?

331
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:54,320
Where did he kick you?

332
00:12:55,790 --> 00:12:56,390
What's wrong?

333
00:12:56,390 --> 00:12:56,920
I'm fine.

334
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:58,180
You... You fell...

335
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:03,140
Careful, Yizhong!

336
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:19,750
Do you know those two

337
00:13:19,750 --> 00:13:21,390
who were involved in the brawl?

338
00:13:21,390 --> 00:13:22,550
What do you mean, "involved in the brawl,"

339
00:13:22,550 --> 00:13:23,360
officer?

340
00:13:23,670 --> 00:13:25,240
We were stopping a crime!

341
00:13:27,150 --> 00:13:28,480
Quite a temper you have.

342
00:13:28,990 --> 00:13:29,510
What?

343
00:13:30,270 --> 00:13:32,130
Are you going to smash my face too?

344
00:13:32,670 --> 00:13:33,600
I wouldn't dare.

345
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:34,750
Zhao.

346
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:36,780
Chief Chen.

347
00:13:38,270 --> 00:13:39,240
Hello, officer.

348
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:39,720
Hello.

349
00:13:39,750 --> 00:13:40,750
I'm from the security office

350
00:13:40,750 --> 00:13:41,390
of People's University
of Political Science and Law.

351
00:13:41,390 --> 00:13:42,030
I rushed over

352
00:13:42,030 --> 00:13:43,430
as soon as I got your call.

353
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:44,320
Those two

354
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:45,910
are students from our university.

355
00:13:45,910 --> 00:13:47,120
Yu Gaoyuan here

356
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,840
is the student union president

357
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:50,970
and also a probationary Party member.

358
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:03,270
You should've asked me for help.

359
00:14:03,270 --> 00:14:03,870
It's fine.

360
00:14:13,270 --> 00:14:14,510
This hot water is for drinking,

361
00:14:14,510 --> 00:14:15,670
not for soaking your feet.

362
00:14:15,670 --> 00:14:17,320
Fetch your own if you want to do that.

363
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:19,080
Come on, I'm on my period.

364
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,550
Her hand is injured.

365
00:14:20,550 --> 00:14:21,610
Can't you see that?

366
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:24,550
It was supposed to be your turn
to fetch hot water today anyway.

367
00:14:24,550 --> 00:14:25,840
It's fine. Let it go.

368
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:28,140
You can't always be like this—

369
00:14:28,790 --> 00:14:30,200
always giving in to other people.

370
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,870
A certain person not only
doesn't appreciate it

371
00:14:31,870 --> 00:14:33,670
but also takes advantage of you.

372
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:42,650
A certain person just left.

373
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:48,940
Do you think...

374
00:14:49,790 --> 00:14:51,240
that incident will affect

375
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:52,170
our internship?

376
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,000
Don't overthink it.

377
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:55,720
Those 2 thugs

378
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:57,320
have already been arrested.

379
00:14:58,910 --> 00:14:59,510
It's fine.

380
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:08,820
Where are they?

381
00:15:09,870 --> 00:15:11,270
They should be here soon.

382
00:15:21,070 --> 00:15:21,930
This is for you.

383
00:15:23,620 --> 00:15:25,620
Thank you for saving Yingjie and me.

384
00:15:29,750 --> 00:15:31,150
Is there mugwort inside?

385
00:15:32,790 --> 00:15:34,320
I asked the school doctor
for dried tangerine peel

386
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:35,320
and aged mugwort.

387
00:15:35,550 --> 00:15:36,960
I also picked some mint leaves.

388
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:38,150
I dried and ground all of them into powder

389
00:15:38,150 --> 00:15:39,680
and put them in this sachet.

390
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:42,510
I saw that you and Chen Yizhong

391
00:15:42,510 --> 00:15:44,240
got bitten by mosquitoes a lot.

392
00:15:44,270 --> 00:15:45,330
Keep this with you.

393
00:15:45,870 --> 00:15:47,130
It repels mosquitoes.

394
00:15:47,630 --> 00:15:49,560
Girls really are more thoughtful.

395
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:54,360
You don't have to be so polite with me,

396
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:54,840
Lihui.

397
00:15:55,550 --> 00:15:56,720
We're classmates.

398
00:15:57,420 --> 00:15:58,720
If anything happens to you,

399
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,440
it's my responsibility to protect you.

400
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:01,320
If you want to say thanks,

401
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:02,030
you should thank Yizhong too.

402
00:16:02,030 --> 00:16:03,230
His hand got pierced.

403
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:04,800
Of course.

404
00:16:05,790 --> 00:16:06,750
I'm grateful to you both.

405
00:16:06,750 --> 00:16:07,610
He gets one too.

406
00:16:08,630 --> 00:16:10,320
Is his also a mosquito repellent sachet?

407
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:10,840
Yes.

408
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:15,010
However,

409
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:17,000
your sachet has

410
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,130
an extra layer of gauze lining inside.

411
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:20,900
It's more durable.

412
00:16:20,910 --> 00:16:22,840
Don't you wear things out quickly?

413
00:16:23,610 --> 00:16:24,500
So I added

414
00:16:24,550 --> 00:16:26,280
an extra layer of gauze lining.

415
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:27,960
You don't want it?

416
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:28,870
I'll take it back then...

417
00:16:28,870 --> 00:16:29,930
I want it, I want it.

418
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:30,560
Thank you.

419
00:16:51,030 --> 00:16:52,440
Why didn't you go to class?

420
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:53,640
I came to check on you.

421
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:54,770
How's your hand?

422
00:16:54,790 --> 00:16:55,360
I'm fine.

423
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:58,910
I brought these for you.

424
00:16:58,910 --> 00:16:59,510
Thanks.

425
00:17:04,829 --> 00:17:05,589
Thirty-two.

426
00:17:09,069 --> 00:17:09,920
What 32?

427
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:11,960
This is the 32nd sentence

428
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:13,640
you've said to me this year.

429
00:17:14,510 --> 00:17:16,710
The previous one was "How's your hand?"

430
00:17:19,030 --> 00:17:20,790
Am I really that bad to you?

431
00:17:21,349 --> 00:17:22,069
Used to it.

432
00:17:23,510 --> 00:17:25,040
Playing the pity card, huh?

433
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:25,680
No.

434
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:27,109
I mean, you've gotten so used to

435
00:17:27,109 --> 00:17:28,170
treating me badly,

436
00:17:28,310 --> 00:17:29,070
you don't even notice anymore.

437
00:17:29,070 --> 00:17:30,330
Then let me praise you.

438
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:32,740
You were really brave.

439
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:35,610
That was justifiable defense.

440
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:36,750
We must

441
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:39,640
learn to think
in terms of legal reasoning.

442
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:47,080
Released?

443
00:17:47,590 --> 00:17:50,200
The one who stabbed him hasn't been released.
He'll be sentenced.

444
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:52,830
The one who was egging things on
got detained for 7 days.

445
00:17:52,830 --> 00:17:53,270
Mr. Hu,

446
00:17:53,270 --> 00:17:54,680
3 to 7 years for the principal offender

447
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:55,790
shouldn't be a problem.

448
00:17:55,790 --> 00:17:57,310
The accessory is guilty of
attempted assault

449
00:17:57,310 --> 00:17:58,920
and hooliganism. How is it...

450
00:17:58,920 --> 00:17:59,920
just a detention?

451
00:18:00,510 --> 00:18:02,000
Even village officials in your hometown

452
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,310
can become local tyrants,

453
00:18:03,310 --> 00:18:04,040
let alone...

454
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:07,440
Mr. Hu, you mean

455
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:08,900
that guy has connections?

456
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,180
Let's not talk about that.

457
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:12,610
This internship

458
00:18:13,110 --> 00:18:14,440
is extremely important

459
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:16,190
for your future job assignments.

460
00:18:16,190 --> 00:18:17,050
Our department

461
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:18,480
has a natural advantage in

462
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:20,010
getting into the SPC and SPP

463
00:18:20,350 --> 00:18:21,980
But if you want things
to naturally fall into place,

464
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:23,980
you still need to put in some effort.

465
00:18:24,350 --> 00:18:25,080
In our class,

466
00:18:25,350 --> 00:18:26,750
I have high hopes for you.

467
00:18:26,790 --> 00:18:27,790
Thank you, Mr. Hu.

468
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:30,850
I come from a rural background myself.

469
00:18:31,070 --> 00:18:33,030
Those feelings bottled up inside you—

470
00:18:33,030 --> 00:18:34,290
I've felt them myself.

471
00:18:34,750 --> 00:18:35,590
Justice has always

472
00:18:35,590 --> 00:18:36,440
come at a cost.

473
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:39,110
Don't be naive...

474
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:42,400
and throw yourself away as that cost.

475
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:43,200
I understand.

476
00:18:43,550 --> 00:18:44,680
If I hadn't learned it the hard way,

477
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:46,410
I wouldn't be telling you this.

478
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:52,100
Come on.

479
00:18:52,350 --> 00:18:52,790
Eat up.

480
00:18:57,110 --> 00:18:58,440
Mr. Hu, I just want to...

481
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:01,960
I just want to

482
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:04,000
contribute something to the advancement

483
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,600
of China's judicial system.

484
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:08,510
At the very least, I want to help

485
00:19:08,510 --> 00:19:10,370
achieve equality before the law.

486
00:19:35,350 --> 00:19:35,960
Mr. Zhou.

487
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:36,920
Yizhong.

488
00:19:37,750 --> 00:19:39,400
This is a compilation of files

489
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:40,400
concerning murder cases

490
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,640
arising from family disputes

491
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:42,790
over the past 5 years.

492
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:44,120
Okay, let me take a look.

493
00:19:48,510 --> 00:19:49,040
Yizhong.

494
00:19:49,550 --> 00:19:50,920
How is your German coming along?

495
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:52,400
I've been memorizing vocabulary every day.

496
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:53,130
It's so hard.

497
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:57,160
Have you told your dad

498
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,530
about studying abroad?

499
00:19:58,590 --> 00:19:59,270
No.

500
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:02,410
I'll tell him when it's a done deal.

501
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:08,480
Back then,

502
00:20:09,110 --> 00:20:10,510
my dad and I were the same.

503
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,260
We argued all the time.

504
00:20:13,310 --> 00:20:14,200
That's how it is

505
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:15,460
for every generation.

506
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,080
Oh, right.

507
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:21,040
How is that hooligan case going?

508
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:23,270
Still waiting for
the first-instance judgment.

509
00:20:23,270 --> 00:20:24,730
Not sure how they'll rule.

510
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:27,880
The public security situation

511
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:28,640
is very grim.

512
00:20:30,310 --> 00:20:31,440
Across the country,

513
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:33,520
appalling and violent crimes

514
00:20:33,520 --> 00:20:35,580
continue to occur one after another.

515
00:20:35,770 --> 00:20:37,160
This isn't merely
an eruption of social pressure

516
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:38,680
accumulated over the past decade or more—

517
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:39,640
it's also the result

518
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:41,900
of a long-term breakdown in legal order.

519
00:20:42,110 --> 00:20:43,170
If this continues,

520
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,070
it will not only affect

521
00:20:44,070 --> 00:20:45,070
reform and opening up

522
00:20:45,070 --> 00:20:47,270
but also make ordinary people feel unsafe.

523
00:20:47,270 --> 00:20:48,160
Yizhong, you're here.

524
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:48,760
Mr. Cheng.

525
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:51,510
You guys talk.

526
00:20:51,510 --> 00:20:52,070
I'll head back.

527
00:20:52,070 --> 00:20:52,930
Okay, go ahead.

528
00:20:59,830 --> 00:21:00,690
Have you heard?

529
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:03,240
What do you think?

530
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:07,500
It's what the situation demands.

531
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:09,790
There's no choice but to do it, I suppose.

532
00:21:09,790 --> 00:21:12,640
The current public security situation
is severe.

533
00:21:13,030 --> 00:21:14,690
A strict crackdown is needed.

534
00:21:14,790 --> 00:21:16,510
But I'm also worried about overcorrecting—

535
00:21:16,510 --> 00:21:18,680
going too far is
as bad as not going far enough.

536
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:20,750
That's especially true
at the grassroots level.

537
00:21:20,750 --> 00:21:23,210
Haven't we learned enough lessons already?

538
00:21:24,550 --> 00:21:25,550
I was thinking...

539
00:21:26,110 --> 00:21:26,510
Well,

540
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:28,000
the students are about to go to

541
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:29,160
the grassroots level
for their internships.

542
00:21:29,160 --> 00:21:31,350
This would be a good chance to conduct

543
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:34,180
some observations and gather information.

544
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:40,880
Comrades,

545
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:42,760
since reform and opening up,

546
00:21:42,790 --> 00:21:44,680
population movement
has increased significantly—

547
00:21:44,680 --> 00:21:46,160
educated youth returning to the cities,

548
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:48,620
surplus laborers flowing into urban areas.

549
00:21:49,070 --> 00:21:51,310
During this transition
between the old and new orders,

550
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:53,160
gaps in governance have emerged,

551
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:56,360
and law and order has deteriorated sharply
in some areas.

552
00:21:56,510 --> 00:21:57,550
Yizhong called.

553
00:21:58,140 --> 00:21:59,510
The call came through at Zhang's place,

554
00:21:59,510 --> 00:22:00,970
so I went over to answer it.

555
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:02,210
I also

556
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:03,970
brought over some of Yizhong's

557
00:22:04,200 --> 00:22:06,400
outgrown clothes for their eldest son.

558
00:22:07,510 --> 00:22:08,370
What did he say?

559
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:10,500
He said the clothes fit him very well.

560
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:12,340
I'm asking what Yizhong said.

561
00:22:13,750 --> 00:22:14,510
He said

562
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:16,590
he's going somewhere in Nanyu

563
00:22:16,590 --> 00:22:18,000
for the internship.

564
00:22:18,740 --> 00:22:20,790
That place seems quite remote.

565
00:22:22,110 --> 00:22:23,240
I also asked around—

566
00:22:23,440 --> 00:22:24,750
apparently the men there

567
00:22:24,750 --> 00:22:25,750
are quite barbaric.

568
00:22:25,750 --> 00:22:27,410
They like to beat their wives.

569
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:29,770
Can you get to the point?

570
00:22:30,070 --> 00:22:31,350
This is the point.

571
00:22:32,070 --> 00:22:32,960
I'm worried he'll

572
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,510
pick up bad habits there.

573
00:22:34,550 --> 00:22:36,200
Eradicating harmful trends

574
