855
00:31:17,160 --> 00:31:18,160
a courtroom here.

856
00:31:18,350 --> 00:31:19,400
When there's a trial,

857
00:31:19,400 --> 00:31:20,200
we set one up in the hallway,

858
00:31:20,200 --> 00:31:21,400
just like that.

859
00:31:21,750 --> 00:31:22,880
If it's windy or raining,

860
00:31:22,880 --> 00:31:24,210
we hold it in the office.

861
00:31:24,550 --> 00:31:25,640
For major trials,

862
00:31:25,790 --> 00:31:27,720
we borrow
the county government's auditorium.

863
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:28,830
For public sentencing rallies,

864
00:31:28,830 --> 00:31:30,760
we hold them in the square outside.

865
00:31:32,150 --> 00:31:33,350
W-W-What is that about?

866
00:31:33,350 --> 00:31:34,550
The trial is about to start.

867
00:31:34,550 --> 00:31:35,010
Really?

868
00:31:35,160 --> 00:31:35,920
That lively?

869
00:31:36,070 --> 00:31:37,270
I-I'll go take a look.

870
00:31:38,960 --> 00:31:39,960
It's a bit shabby.

871
00:31:52,750 --> 00:31:54,160
What are you doing? What are you doing?

872
00:31:54,160 --> 00:31:55,440
W-W-What are you doing?

873
00:31:55,440 --> 00:31:56,850
Stop this! This is a courtroom!

874
00:31:56,850 --> 00:31:57,580
Pick that up!

875
00:31:57,830 --> 00:31:58,290
Enough!

876
00:32:00,920 --> 00:32:02,320
Enough, enough, enough.

877
00:32:07,640 --> 00:32:08,160
Um...

878
00:32:09,030 --> 00:32:10,110
About the defense statement,

879
00:32:10,110 --> 00:32:11,030
it's due on Monday.

880
00:32:11,030 --> 00:32:12,000
Give it to me by Saturday.

881
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:14,030
So I can review it
before passing it to the director.

882
00:32:14,030 --> 00:32:15,030
I'm currently

883
00:32:15,030 --> 00:32:16,750
busy with Qiao Zhiliang's case.

884
00:32:16,750 --> 00:32:18,070
Why don't you ask Qin

885
00:32:18,070 --> 00:32:19,000
to write it for you?

886
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:19,350
Who?

887
00:32:19,750 --> 00:32:20,240
Qin.

888
00:32:22,680 --> 00:32:23,210
Comrade.

889
00:32:23,640 --> 00:32:24,170
Comrade.

890
00:32:24,810 --> 00:32:27,850
Well, you're
the plaintiff's representative,

891
00:32:27,880 --> 00:32:28,280
right?

892
00:32:30,790 --> 00:32:31,550
The defendant.

893
00:32:31,550 --> 00:32:33,750
Well, he took the nameplate over there.

894
00:32:34,400 --> 00:32:36,060
Then why does it sound like...

895
00:32:36,560 --> 00:32:38,000
you and the opposing counsel

896
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:39,350
are from the same unit?

897
00:32:42,440 --> 00:32:42,790
I...

898
00:32:43,310 --> 00:32:44,030
We're both from

899
00:32:44,030 --> 00:32:45,560
the Legal Advisory Office.

900
00:32:46,160 --> 00:32:47,160
That's not right.

901
00:32:47,440 --> 00:32:48,590
How can lawyers from the same unit

902
00:32:48,590 --> 00:32:49,850
represent both sides?

903
00:32:49,880 --> 00:32:51,680
Isn't there a conflict of interest?

904
00:32:51,680 --> 00:32:52,750
C-Conflict of what?

905
00:32:52,750 --> 00:32:54,010
Conflict of interest.

906
00:32:54,400 --> 00:32:54,960
I mean,

907
00:32:55,350 --> 00:32:57,150
how can both parties in a dispute

908
00:32:57,270 --> 00:32:59,070
use lawyers from the same organization?

909
00:32:59,070 --> 00:33:00,200
No, you see, well...

910
00:33:01,790 --> 00:33:02,440
Our county

911
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:04,520
only has this one Legal Advisory Office.

912
00:33:04,520 --> 00:33:05,720
When ordinary people
get involved in lawsuits,

913
00:33:05,720 --> 00:33:07,720
they basically don't hire lawyers.

914
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:08,480
So,

915
00:33:08,510 --> 00:33:09,240
to help develop

916
00:33:09,240 --> 00:33:10,680
the legal system in our county,

917
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:12,640
we're assigned to represent them.

918
00:33:12,750 --> 00:33:14,280
It's mostly free of charge.

919
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:16,630
Quiet.

920
00:33:21,840 --> 00:33:22,560
[Plaintiff]

921
00:33:22,790 --> 00:33:23,920
You... Give it to me!

922
00:33:25,110 --> 00:33:25,510
This... You...

923
00:33:25,510 --> 00:33:26,370
Stop fighting! Stop fighting!

924
00:33:26,370 --> 00:33:27,070
S-Sit down!

925
00:33:27,070 --> 00:33:28,550
Isn't it just a nameplate?

926
00:33:28,680 --> 00:33:29,680
Why fight over it?

927
00:33:30,880 --> 00:33:32,000
Isn't the defendant

928
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:33,050
disrupting court order?

929
00:33:33,050 --> 00:33:33,680
Why isn't

930
00:33:33,680 --> 00:33:35,110
the judge taking any measures?

931
00:33:35,110 --> 00:33:35,970
What measures?

932
00:33:36,070 --> 00:33:38,470
At the very least,
there should be a warning

933
00:33:38,510 --> 00:33:39,480
or a reprimand.

934
00:33:39,750 --> 00:33:40,550
We have to maintain

935
00:33:40,550 --> 00:33:42,210
the seriousness of the court.

936
00:33:44,110 --> 00:33:45,160
I am the plaintiff!

937
00:33:45,160 --> 00:33:46,350
If he takes my nameplate,

938
00:33:46,350 --> 00:33:47,920
wouldn't I become the defendant?

939
00:33:47,920 --> 00:33:49,020
I'm obviously the one in the right!

940
00:33:49,020 --> 00:33:50,350
He's just the guilty party
filing the suit first!

941
00:33:50,350 --> 00:33:51,110
Now, he's the plaintiff.

942
00:33:51,110 --> 00:33:53,240
How come I get to become the defendant?

943
00:33:53,720 --> 00:33:54,680
We're all from the same village.

944
00:33:54,680 --> 00:33:56,010
It's not that big a deal.

945
00:33:56,240 --> 00:33:57,510
Then what would be a big deal?

946
00:33:57,510 --> 00:33:58,770
Assaulting the judge?

947
00:33:59,070 --> 00:33:59,800
I'll hit you!

948
00:34:00,440 --> 00:34:01,240
Don't use violence!

949
00:34:01,240 --> 00:34:02,680
Don't be so sharp with your words.

950
00:34:02,680 --> 00:34:03,610
Enough! Enough!

951
00:34:05,030 --> 00:34:07,030
This is a court! This is a courtroom!

952
00:34:07,110 --> 00:34:08,360
This is outrageous!

953
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:10,000
Both of you, listen to me!

954
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:10,530
Today...

955
00:34:11,360 --> 00:34:12,420
we're adjourning.

956
00:34:12,590 --> 00:34:13,510
We'll resume the trial

957
00:34:13,510 --> 00:34:15,070
after we resolve this issue.

958
00:34:15,070 --> 00:34:16,330
Give me the nameplate!

959
00:34:20,110 --> 00:34:20,550
Zhang!

960
00:34:21,040 --> 00:34:21,889
Zhang, Zhang.

961
00:34:21,920 --> 00:34:22,380
Come on.

962
00:34:22,880 --> 00:34:23,810
Come on, come on.

963
00:34:23,920 --> 00:34:25,120
Let me introduce you.

964
00:34:25,960 --> 00:34:26,560
Students,

965
00:34:26,760 --> 00:34:28,360
this is Zhang, Zhang Encheng.

966
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:29,110
From now on,

967
00:34:29,840 --> 00:34:31,100
he will be your mentor.

968
00:34:31,150 --> 00:34:32,480
Don't call me "mentor."

969
00:34:33,590 --> 00:34:35,150
Court Pres. Ding, I told you already.

970
00:34:35,150 --> 00:34:36,110
With my level of ability,

971
00:34:36,110 --> 00:34:37,880
I can't mentor college students.

972
00:34:37,880 --> 00:34:39,190
Your ability is excellent.

973
00:34:39,190 --> 00:34:40,110
Let me tell you,

974
00:34:40,110 --> 00:34:40,909
he is one of our

975
00:34:41,090 --> 00:34:42,610
most experienced

976
00:34:42,880 --> 00:34:44,150
presiding judges here.

977
00:34:44,150 --> 00:34:45,350
Many ordinary people

978
00:34:45,550 --> 00:34:47,550
call h-h-him

979
00:34:48,440 --> 00:34:49,770
"Upright Judge Zhang."

980
00:34:50,480 --> 00:34:51,739
Take good care of them.

981
00:34:51,760 --> 00:34:53,190
Let's exchange ideas
and learn from each other.

982
00:34:53,190 --> 00:34:53,550
Okay.

983
00:34:53,670 --> 00:34:54,280
I'll leave you to it.

984
00:34:54,280 --> 00:34:54,670
Okay.

985
00:34:56,440 --> 00:34:56,920
Mentor.

986
00:34:57,670 --> 00:34:59,070
I saw things getting heated

987
00:34:59,070 --> 00:35:00,230
right in the court just now.

988
00:35:00,230 --> 00:35:01,400
Is it always like this?

989
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:02,760
Ordinary people.

990
00:35:03,400 --> 00:35:05,400
They aren't used to dealing with the law.

991
00:35:05,400 --> 00:35:06,480
They think

992
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:09,240
being a defendant is a disgrace.

993
00:35:09,670 --> 00:35:13,000
They believe that being the defendant
is the same as being guilty.

994
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:13,800
What can we do?

995
00:35:14,070 --> 00:35:15,470
Next time we hold a trial,

996
00:35:16,150 --> 00:35:18,150
we just won't put out
those two nameplates.

997
00:35:18,150 --> 00:35:19,680
Not put out the nameplates?

998
00:35:20,400 --> 00:35:21,920
Will not putting out nameplates

999
00:35:21,920 --> 00:35:23,120
affect the judgment?

1000
00:35:23,400 --> 00:35:24,500
It won't affect it,

1001
00:35:24,590 --> 00:35:25,030
but...

1002
00:35:25,030 --> 00:35:25,830
Well, Mentor,

1003
00:35:25,880 --> 00:35:27,110
I think whether it affects the judgment

1004
00:35:27,110 --> 00:35:27,840
is one thing,

1005
00:35:28,110 --> 00:35:29,030
but the dignity of the law

1006
00:35:29,030 --> 00:35:29,880
is another.

1007
00:35:29,880 --> 00:35:30,610
So I think...

1008
00:35:32,030 --> 00:35:32,430
Zhang,

1009
00:35:32,710 --> 00:35:33,550
the accused has been brought in.

1010
00:35:33,550 --> 00:35:34,920
Are we ready to begin the trial?

1011
00:35:34,920 --> 00:35:35,760
He's already here?

1012
00:35:35,760 --> 00:35:36,570
No, h-hurry up!

1013
00:35:36,570 --> 00:35:37,030
Well...

1014
00:35:37,070 --> 00:35:38,070
Um... Zheng.

1015
00:35:38,190 --> 00:35:39,170
Go check

1016
00:35:39,320 --> 00:35:40,190
if the assessors have arrived.

1017
00:35:40,190 --> 00:35:40,550
Okay.

1018
00:35:46,550 --> 00:35:47,010
Mentor.

1019
00:35:47,030 --> 00:35:47,590
You're still...

1020
00:35:47,590 --> 00:35:48,150
W-What kind of case

1021
00:35:48,150 --> 00:35:49,480
are you going to try now?

1022
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:50,860
A robbery case.

1023
00:35:51,150 --> 00:35:52,000
You preside over

1024
00:35:52,000 --> 00:35:53,320
both criminal and civil cases?

1025
00:35:53,320 --> 00:35:54,070
Here,

1026
00:35:54,330 --> 00:35:56,060
we have more cases than judges.

1027
00:35:56,360 --> 00:35:57,770
Whether it's criminal or civil,

1028
00:35:57,770 --> 00:36:00,170
we have to take
whatever cases come our way.

1029
00:36:00,460 --> 00:36:01,930
[Prosecutor]

1030
00:36:02,200 --> 00:36:03,850
[Defense Counsel]

1031
00:36:11,670 --> 00:36:12,320
Quiet.

1032
00:36:13,920 --> 00:36:15,850
The People's Court of Nanyu County

1033
00:36:15,920 --> 00:36:17,160
is now hearing in public

1034
00:36:17,160 --> 00:36:18,680
the case brought by

1035
00:36:18,710 --> 00:36:20,030
the Nanyu County People's Procuratorate

1036
00:36:20,030 --> 00:36:21,960
against Liu Erlin for armed robbery.

1037
00:36:21,960 --> 00:36:23,330
The court is now in session.

1038
00:36:23,330 --> 00:36:25,190
There really are judges who preside over

1039
00:36:25,190 --> 00:36:26,440
both civil and criminal divisions,

1040
00:36:26,440 --> 00:36:28,110
and lawyers often switch roles as needed.

1041
00:36:28,110 --> 00:36:29,710
Well, that's an eye-opener.

1042
00:36:34,840 --> 00:36:36,150
Uncle Zhang, we meet again.

1043
00:36:36,150 --> 00:36:36,810
Be serious.

1044
00:36:39,490 --> 00:36:42,920
[Defendant]

1045
00:36:39,710 --> 00:36:40,970
Defendant, your name?

1046
00:36:42,280 --> 00:36:42,880
Liu Erlin.

1047
00:36:43,960 --> 00:36:44,400
Age?

1048
00:36:44,630 --> 00:36:45,360
Twenty-six.

1049
00:36:48,710 --> 00:36:50,440
The defendant disregarded the law,

1050
00:36:50,440 --> 00:36:51,560
impersonated a police officer,

1051
00:36:51,560 --> 00:36:52,670
and committed armed robbery

1052
00:36:52,670 --> 00:36:53,730
in broad daylight.

1053
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:55,190
Although the firearm he carried

1054
00:36:55,190 --> 00:36:55,920
was a toy gun,

1055
00:36:56,190 --> 00:36:57,670
that does not change the fact

1056
00:36:57,670 --> 00:36:59,710
that his actions
constituted armed robbery.

1057
00:36:59,710 --> 00:37:01,510
The defendant has a prior criminal record

1058
00:37:01,510 --> 00:37:02,800
for theft,

1059
00:37:03,030 --> 00:37:04,670
making him a repeat offender.

1060
00:37:04,670 --> 00:37:05,880
Do you think Mr. Zhou and Mr. Cheng

1061
00:37:05,880 --> 00:37:07,710
know that it's like this
here in the rural areas?

1062
00:37:07,710 --> 00:37:08,280
Listen, listen.

1063
00:37:08,280 --> 00:37:10,070
The crime is particularly serious.

1064
00:37:10,070 --> 00:37:12,120
He must receive
severe punishment under the law.

1065
00:37:12,120 --> 00:37:12,920
No, wait. How can you

1066
00:37:12,920 --> 00:37:13,980
wrong me like this?

1067
00:37:14,030 --> 00:37:15,210
How did I commit a crime?

1068
00:37:15,210 --> 00:37:16,710
Why should I be severely punished?

1069
00:37:16,710 --> 00:37:17,370
Defendant,

1070
00:37:17,760 --> 00:37:18,510
no shouting.

1071
00:37:19,150 --> 00:37:21,350
Speak only when the court allows you to.

1072
00:37:23,390 --> 00:37:26,050
Defense counsel,
please present your defense.

1073
00:37:29,590 --> 00:37:30,840
Honorable Presiding Judge,

1074
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:32,040
People's Assessors,

1075
00:37:32,590 --> 00:37:33,760
I have been entrusted

1076
00:37:33,760 --> 00:37:35,150
by the defendant Liu Erlin

1077
00:37:35,150 --> 00:37:35,800
and assigned by the Nanyu County

1078
00:37:35,800 --> 00:37:37,060
Legal Advisory Office

1079
00:37:37,410 --> 00:37:38,840
to appear in court today, together with

1080
00:37:38,840 --> 00:37:39,900
Attorney Li Xiang,

1081
00:37:39,960 --> 00:37:43,070
to enter a plea
for a lighter sentence for the defendant.

1082
00:37:43,070 --> 00:37:43,670
Regarding

1083
00:37:44,440 --> 00:37:44,840
the prosecution's...

1084
00:37:44,840 --> 00:37:45,360
There's one knitting.

1085
00:37:45,360 --> 00:37:46,400
Statement just now...

1086
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:47,000
We believe

1087
00:37:47,360 --> 00:37:48,760
the basic facts are clear

1088
00:37:48,840 --> 00:37:49,590
and the evidence largely conclusive.

1089
00:37:49,590 --> 00:37:50,380
There's one smoking.

1090
00:37:50,380 --> 00:37:50,910
However,

1091
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:52,280
we must

1092
00:37:52,440 --> 00:37:54,040
specifically point out that

1093
00:37:54,440 --> 00:37:55,590
although the defendant in this case

1094
00:37:55,590 --> 00:37:56,550
did commit

1095
00:37:56,600 --> 00:37:57,880
the criminal acts as charged by

1096
00:37:57,880 --> 00:37:58,800
the prosecution,

1097
00:37:58,800 --> 00:38:00,800
due to the victim's resistance

1098
00:38:00,880 --> 00:38:01,540
and escape,

1099
00:38:01,780 --> 00:38:03,190
the defendant's robbery objective

1100
00:38:03,190 --> 00:38:04,190
was not achieved.

1101
00:38:04,480 --> 00:38:06,310
Therefore, this should be considered
an attempted crime.

1102
00:38:06,310 --> 00:38:08,190
[Presiding Judge, People's Assessor]

1103
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:07,760
Furthermore,

1104
00:38:08,020 --> 00:38:11,280
the defendant is an occasional offender
and a first-time offender.

1105
00:38:11,280 --> 00:38:14,140
He's a repeat offender,
not a first-time offender.

1106
00:38:19,110 --> 00:38:21,840
Although the defendant...
is a repeat offender,

1107
00:38:23,110 --> 00:38:24,880
he has deeply repented

1108
00:38:25,550 --> 00:38:26,840
and truthfully confessed

1109
00:38:26,840 --> 00:38:27,670
his entire crime

1110
00:38:27,670 --> 00:38:29,070
to the public security authorities.

1111
00:38:29,070 --> 00:38:30,030
His attitude toward admitting guilt
is fairly good...

1112
00:38:30,030 --> 00:38:31,280
His attitude is not good.

1113
00:38:31,280 --> 00:38:32,610
I haven't finished yet!

1114
00:38:34,550 --> 00:38:37,210
I hope the court
will impose a lighter sentence.

1115
00:38:38,550 --> 00:38:39,920
There's no room for "lighter."

1116
00:38:39,920 --> 00:38:41,720
He still hasn't admitted guilt.

1117
00:38:41,800 --> 00:38:42,530
Prosecutor,

1118
00:38:43,030 --> 00:38:44,400
you may speak

1119
00:38:44,400 --> 00:38:45,800
during the court debate.

1120
00:38:47,480 --> 00:38:48,140
Defendant,

1121
00:38:48,960 --> 00:38:50,490
do you have anything to say?

1122
00:38:50,840 --> 00:38:51,840
Presiding Judge,

1123
00:38:52,030 --> 00:38:54,630
I-I-I'm innocent!
I really didn't rob anyone.

1124
00:38:54,740 --> 00:38:56,070
I was just joking with that guy.

1125
00:38:56,070 --> 00:38:56,920
I mistook him for someone else.

1126
00:38:56,920 --> 00:38:57,810
I took the toy gun

1127
00:38:57,810 --> 00:38:58,920
and poked him in the lower back.

1128
00:38:58,920 --> 00:38:59,940
When he turned around, I realized

1129
00:38:59,940 --> 00:39:01,030
I had the wrong person.

1130
00:39:01,030 --> 00:39:01,670
Besides,

1131
00:39:01,710 --> 00:39:02,630
even if I had robbed someone,

1132
00:39:02,630 --> 00:39:04,400
who would do it
in the middle of the street?

1133
00:39:04,400 --> 00:39:05,760
Just now, he said
I refused to admit my crime.

1134
00:39:05,760 --> 00:39:06,480
I didn't commit a crime,

1135
00:39:06,480 --> 00:39:07,960
so what guilt would I admit?

1136
00:39:07,960 --> 00:39:10,360
Please present the evidence, Prosecutor.

1137
00:39:11,080 --> 00:39:12,800
We have collected the police uniform

1138
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:15,100
the defendant wore during the robbery,

1139
00:39:15,470 --> 00:39:17,320
as well as the toy gun

1140
00:39:17,440 --> 00:39:18,770
and holster he carried.

1141
00:39:19,070 --> 00:39:21,400
Bailiff, please submit them to the court.

1142
00:39:29,000 --> 00:39:30,360
I bought this uniform at the market

1143
00:39:30,360 --> 00:39:31,230
for 6 yuan.

1144
00:39:31,480 --> 00:39:32,190
The gun is mine,

1145
00:39:32,190 --> 00:39:33,520
but this holster isn't.

1146
00:39:33,880 --> 00:39:36,140
You're saying this holster isn't yours?

1147
00:39:36,440 --> 00:39:37,320
I just bought mine, so it's new,

1148
00:39:37,320 --> 00:39:39,320
while this one's all worn and peeling.

1149
00:39:39,320 --> 00:39:40,050
Prosecutor,

1150
00:39:40,480 --> 00:39:41,680
what's going on here?

1151
00:39:41,710 --> 00:39:42,170
Well...

1152
00:39:42,230 --> 00:39:44,000
When the police transferred him over,

1153
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:46,200
this was the holster that came with him.

1154
00:39:51,280 --> 00:39:51,960
This really is not

1155
00:39:51,960 --> 00:39:53,220
the holster he bought.

1156
00:39:53,550 --> 00:39:55,010
Then where is his holster?

1157
00:39:55,480 --> 00:39:56,540
It's at our bureau.

1158
00:39:56,920 --> 00:39:58,230
My old holster was too worn out,

1159
00:39:58,230 --> 00:39:59,090
so I swapped it.

1160
00:40:00,070 --> 00:40:01,800
This is evidence for the court.

1161
00:40:02,110 --> 00:40:03,580
Stop laughing. Be serious.

1162
00:40:03,580 --> 00:40:04,960
They're all just holsters anyway.

1163
00:40:04,960 --> 00:40:06,360
Once it's just sitting in the court
as evidence,

1164
00:40:06,360 --> 00:40:07,160
it's useless.

1165
00:40:07,470 --> 00:40:09,730
I was just thinking about not wasting it.

1166
00:40:10,150 --> 00:40:10,880
Nonsense.

1167
00:40:13,010 --> 00:40:14,140
It's simply...

1168
00:40:17,360 --> 00:40:18,880
Sis, you take such good care of us.

1169
00:40:18,880 --> 00:40:19,480
Thank you.

1170
00:40:19,510 --> 00:40:20,400
You're welcome.

1171
00:40:20,400 --> 00:40:21,210
We won't eat for free.

1172
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:22,400
We'll buy groceries for you later!

1173
00:40:22,400 --> 00:40:23,330
You're welcome.

1174
00:40:28,190 --> 00:40:29,000
What a feast.

1175
00:40:30,510 --> 00:40:31,170
Here you go.

1176
00:40:32,230 --> 00:40:33,190
Here, tomatoes.

1177
00:40:38,230 --> 00:40:39,320
Those two lawyers' defense statements

1178
00:40:39,320 --> 00:40:40,780
were printed out long ago.

1179
00:40:41,110 --> 00:40:42,570
Only the defendant's name

1180
00:40:42,920 --> 00:40:44,000
was filled in by hand.

1181
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:45,530
Same old script every time.

1182
00:40:45,760 --> 00:40:48,800
Whoever they defend,
they use the exact same template.

1183
00:40:48,800 --> 00:40:49,760
I feel like what we watched today

1184
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:50,560
wasn't a trial

1185
00:40:51,400 --> 00:40:53,000
but a magical realist novel.

1186
00:40:53,670 --> 00:40:55,000
It's only the first day.

1187
00:40:56,190 --> 00:40:57,720
Given what happened today,

1188
00:40:59,030 --> 00:40:59,880
do you think our country

1189
00:40:59,880 --> 00:41:02,010
can really move toward the rule of law?

1190
00:41:06,400 --> 00:41:07,600
As the ancients said,

1191
00:41:07,710 --> 00:41:09,710
"Law is the scale of a state

1192
00:41:09,900 --> 00:41:10,780
and the ethical benchmark for a society—

1193
00:41:10,780 --> 00:41:12,590
a vital instrument
for governing the country."

1194
00:41:12,590 --> 00:41:13,280
We were born

1195
00:41:13,280 --> 00:41:14,410
into this great era,

1196
00:41:15,190 --> 00:41:16,150
so of course we must take the advancement
of the rule of law

1197
00:41:16,150 --> 00:41:17,480
as our responsibility.

1198
00:41:17,880 --> 00:41:19,550
This is a responsibility and a mission

1199
00:41:19,550 --> 00:41:20,400
that we cannot avoid,

1200
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:22,200
nor do we have the right to avoid.

1201
00:41:24,280 --> 00:41:25,010
I have to say,

1202
00:41:26,280 --> 00:41:26,920
your words really

1203
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:27,880
get me fired up.

1204
00:41:29,190 --> 00:41:29,920
Impressive.

1205
00:41:30,280 --> 00:41:31,410
Really impressive.

1206
00:41:32,470 --> 00:41:34,870
Spoken like a true high-ranking official.

1207
00:41:35,870 --> 00:41:37,310
You're deliberately being cynical,

1208
00:41:37,310 --> 00:41:38,030
avoiding anything lofty

1209
00:41:38,030 --> 00:41:39,830
just to show how special you are.

1210
00:41:39,880 --> 00:41:40,480
Lu Zeming,

1211
00:41:40,710 --> 00:41:42,240
actually, you have ideals.

1212
00:41:46,110 --> 00:41:47,440
Of course I have ideals.

1213
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:50,630
In my heart,

1214
00:41:51,550 --> 00:41:53,080
I always keep the people...

1215
00:41:53,960 --> 00:41:54,890
and their money.

1216
00:41:56,150 --> 00:41:57,440
My mind is full of money.

1217
00:41:57,440 --> 00:41:58,900
All I think about is money.

1218
00:42:03,030 --> 00:42:04,290
I'm not as noble as you.

1219
00:42:04,670 --> 00:42:07,330
And all that...
that "vital instrument" stuff.

1220
00:42:12,230 --> 00:42:12,920
Give it back!

1221
00:42:12,920 --> 00:42:13,590
Give my stuff back!

1222
00:42:13,590 --> 00:42:14,840
Slow down! Don't fall!

1223
00:42:14,840 --> 00:42:15,440
Slow down.

1224
00:42:15,840 --> 00:42:18,150
Hurry up! Give it back. Give it back!

1225
00:42:18,320 --> 00:42:19,150
I won't!

1226
00:42:20,110 --> 00:42:21,320
Come on, come. It's here.

1227
00:42:21,320 --> 00:42:22,150
That's mine!

1228
00:42:22,150 --> 00:42:23,110
-Hurry up!
-I won't!

1229
00:42:23,110 --> 00:42:24,360
I won't! I won't!

1230
00:42:24,670 --> 00:42:27,360
Alright, alright! Enough!

1231
00:42:27,840 --> 00:42:29,070
Give it back!

1232
00:42:29,510 --> 00:42:30,550
Quiet! Quiet!

1233
00:42:30,670 --> 00:42:31,730
Quiet. Quiet down!

1234
00:42:31,800 --> 00:42:32,550
Everyone, quiet now!

1235
00:42:32,550 --> 00:42:34,110
Your place is the liveliest of all.

1236
00:42:34,110 --> 00:42:35,320
Court Pres. Ding, let me tell you.

1237
00:42:35,320 --> 00:42:36,580
I didn't delay my work.

1238
00:42:36,840 --> 00:42:38,390
His fever is already gone.

1239
00:42:38,410 --> 00:42:39,840
I'll take them back at noon.

1240
00:42:39,840 --> 00:42:41,550
You can't always spoil him.

1241
00:42:42,000 --> 00:42:42,480
Get out!

1242
00:42:42,760 --> 00:42:44,420
Come on, let me introduce you.

1243
00:42:44,840 --> 00:42:45,630
These two

1244
00:42:46,030 --> 00:42:48,510
are top students from
the University of Political Science and Law.

1245
00:42:48,510 --> 00:42:49,590
This is Xia.

1246
00:42:50,230 --> 00:42:51,160
I'm Xia Yingjie.

1247
00:42:51,760 --> 00:42:52,890
This is Zhang.

1248
00:42:52,960 --> 00:42:53,800
I'm Zhang Lihui.

1249
00:42:53,800 --> 00:42:54,530
This is Fang,

1250
00:42:54,670 --> 00:42:56,010
no, Fang Shumei.

1251
00:42:56,230 --> 00:42:56,840
You'll be interning here

1252
00:42:56,840 --> 00:42:57,630
for a year,

1253
00:42:58,000 --> 00:42:58,940
and Fang will

1254
00:42:59,000 --> 00:43:00,200
serve as your mentor.

1255
00:43:00,630 --> 00:43:01,440
-Hello, Mentor.
-Hello, Mentor.
